From 7e01f463c3ceb63903ab1d9b317fbfe51f2c6a3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:54:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(post): refuse a C-turning rapid when the machine
 states no C rate, with or without a C travel

#906 refused a C-section rapid that turns C only when the machine
states a C travel but no C rate. A machine that states neither (the
c_axis_live bench) still posted its C-turning link rapids at the max
linear feed scaled by the C turn - an uncapped F. The lathe post now
refuses that rapid by name whenever no C rate is stated.

The c_axis_live bench now states a C rate (6000/12000 deg/min, the
shipped millturn.mch's figures) so its contour keeps posting, with every
F checked inside the stated rates; the no-rate case is pinned on an
unrated copy. No golden moves.

Fixes #966

